Function best_catalog_entity_fuzzy_match:
- expose the existing fuzzy catalog ranking as a reusable top-1 helper for other backend layers
- return the highest-ranked candidate or `None` when no reasonable fuzzy candidate survives filtering


Function rank_catalog_entities:
- build the shared ranked candidate list using optional lexical scoring plus the blended `fuzzywuzzy` score
- keep the same ordering and score thresholds used by tool-side search and slug resolution


Function _best_fuzzy_match:
- compare one raw query against one catalog entity across multiple normalized search terms
- blend ratio, partial, token-sort, token-set, and WRatio into one composite fuzzy score


Function _collapsed_lookup_text:
- normalize whitespace and case for the fuzzy matching helper


Class CatalogToolset:
- expose bounded read-only catalog helpers for champions, items, runes, batch lookups, and search
- route all slug lookups through the in-memory catalog snapshot
- return documented ToolView payloads instead of raw catalog payloads
- rank fuzzy name matches with a blended `fuzzywuzzy` score so near-miss IDs like `wr-ludens-echo` still land on the real catalog slug
- build selector candidate pools by combining exactish overlap hits with fuzzy top-20 matches before asking the small selector model to choose one ID
- return explicit `id` fields, top-match detail, and category-based item-ID listings so the main model can see the real catalog identifiers directly
- treat multi-category `list_item_ids` requests as a union of category buckets rather than an impossible intersection
- keep batch/search helpers capped and stable so model-visible tool usage stays bounded
- keep tool behavior deterministic and side-effect free
